## Root cause

Owner: **the tool**. ASG `src/ai_strategy_generator/executability/receipt.py:27-34,96-110` excludes four progress fields from existing registry rows, but hashes every remaining key and row. The worker added `STORE_XDUO_0001` to `specs/0050/.contracts-json:2-9`, recording `lifecycle: implemented`, `implementStep: 69`, `declaringStep: null` and empty consumers/temporaries. Its residual identity is the new id plus `declaringStep: null` and `consumers: []`. This is the **only** changed receipt input. ASG `multistep/implement_contract_worker.system-md:25-33` requires the lifecycle update, while `step_compiler/compile.py:940-1044` explicitly permits inherited contracts without an arc-local row. `compile_spec` publishes a receipt without preparing that row; `multistep/_arc_runner/runtime/run_arc_runner.py:4408-4411` rejects its subsequent creation before any feedback build or review. These contracts conflict at first implementation of an inherited seam.

This extends an already diagnosed tool defect: ASG `specs/0090/.manual/017-cleaned-hashes-and-registry-progress-fix-log.md` records the same trigger for STL's implementation worker. The November 1 fix, commit `dd03dc3a`, handled changes within existing rows. Its test deliberately rejects a new id, without distinguishing an unplanned identity from a globally registered, published-plan inherited contract. Berreman 0069 reaches that missing case. No evidence points to a product failure, prompt change, whitespace drift or model change as the escalation's cause. Product correctness still requires the unrun review and acceptance roster.

